## Source
Path A UX dry-run (0152), severity: **Medium**

## Context
The README uses `tickets/erg init`, `tickets/erg new`, etc. without explaining
why the binary lives inside `tickets/` rather than globally. A developer with a
global `erg` will wonder which one runs; a new user won't understand the design.

The reason matters: per-project bootstrap so every repo carries its own pinned
binary — no version skew across machines or teammates.

## Fix
Add ≤2 sentences in the install section or Binary policy callout:
"The binary lives in `tickets/erg` rather than a global path so each project
carries its own pinned version — everyone uses the same binary without a
separate install step."

## Exit criteria
- [ ] README explains the per-project binary rationale in ≤2 sentences
